PRIVACY = """PIXEL is the SAIT college photography and social platform managed by the college social media club.

Accounts are limited to verified @sait.ac.in addresses. We process your college email, chosen username, password hash (for password accounts), profile details, authentication sessions, policy acknowledgements and security audit records to operate and protect your account. Google sign-in shares a verified college email and Google account identifier with PIXEL; your Google password is never shared with us. Other signed-in college members can see your username, display name, department, year and bio after onboarding. Your email and security records are not included in public profiles.

Only Administrators publish application content and manage accounts. Student and Faculty users can manage their own profiles and permitted interactions. Do not put sensitive personal information in your public bio.

Find Yourself face processing is a separate feature. Acknowledging this policy does not grant biometric consent. Face matching will require a separate notice and explicit consent before it is enabled. It is not active in this authentication release.

Use the account settings or contact pixel.club@sait.ac.in for account, correction or deletion requests. Authentication sessions expire after seven days or are revoked on logout; expired authentication artifacts are removed by scheduled cleanup. Account records remain while the account is active. Security audit records are retained for up to 90 days. Deleting an account removes its authentication and profile records; any future content, backup or biometric retention rules must be disclosed before those features launch.

This is the development privacy notice for the implemented account features. The college must approve the final privacy contact, retention and deployment disclosures before public release."""

TERMS = """Use PIXEL only with your own SAIT college account. Keep your credentials private, use a username that does not impersonate another person, and treat other members respectfully. Do not harass users, misuse photographs, attempt unauthorized downloads or publish content without permission. Only the college's authorized Administrators manage published content. The social media club may suspend accounts that violate campus rules. Photography rights, production support procedures and final college terms must be approved before public release."""
